{{/*
  tier-check — the visible "Tier check" preamble used by every beads-issues
  **phase** prompt to declare which model tier it expects (Reasoning or
  Coding) and to gracefully surface a tier-degraded run when the
  transient `preferredModels` switch did not land.

  Consumers: feature-phase-plan / -implement / -test / -review,
  fix-phase-reproduce / -investigate / -fix.

  Callers first resolve the target bead into a local `$target` (same
  variable already used for `target-bead-header-strict`), then invoke:

      {{ template "beads-issues/shared/tier-check" (dict
          "Target"    $target
          "Tier"      "Reasoning"
          "Phase"     "plan"
          "Confirmed" (Model "Reasoning")
          "ModelName" .Session.ModelName
          "ModelTags" .Session.ModelTags
      ) }}

  Parameters:
    Target    — the resolved bead ID (used inside the tier-degraded
                `bd comment` command). Callers reuse the same `$target`
                variable already set for target-bead-header-strict.
    Tier      — the declared tier tag: `"Reasoning"` or `"Coding"`.
    Phase     — the short phase name shown inside the tier-degraded
                `[phase: <phase>]` marker (e.g. `"plan"`, `"implement"`,
                `"test"`, `"review"`, `"reproduce"`, `"investigate"`,
                `"fix"`).
    Confirmed — bool; true when the active model carries the .Tier tag.
                Callers must pass `(Model .Tier)` from the outer context
                because `Model` is not in the narrow FuncMap that
                target.title templates use (see internal/prompts/target.go),
                and every fragment is attached to every render — so the
                fragment itself may not reference `Model`.
    ModelName — pass through `.Session.ModelName` so the degraded-run
                comment can name the running model.
    ModelTags — pass through `.Session.ModelTags` so the degraded-run
                comment can enumerate the running model's tags.

  Branches:
    * .Confirmed == true:
        "✓ <Tier> tier confirmed — proceed."
    * else (tier-degraded):
        "⚠ **Tier-degraded run.** … bd comment <target> \"⚠ tier-degraded
         [phase: <phase>]: declared <Tier> but running on '<model>' (tags:
         <tags>).\""

  The fragment is self-contained (balanced `{{ if }}/{{ end }}`) and uses
  ONLY builtin text/template actions (no external funcs), so it is safe to
  attach to every render — including the narrow-FuncMap target.title path.
*/}}
## Tier check

This phase is declared to run on the **{{ .Tier }}** tier (`preferredModels: [{modelTag: {{ .Tier }}}]`).
Active model: `{{ if .ModelName }}{{ .ModelName }}{{ else }}<unknown>{{ end }}` (tags: {{ if .ModelTags }}{{ range $i, $t := .ModelTags }}{{ if $i }}, {{ end }}{{ $t }}{{ end }}{{ else }}none{{ end }}).

{{ if .Confirmed -}}
✓ {{ .Tier }} tier confirmed — proceed.
{{- else -}}
⚠ **Tier-degraded run.** The active model does not carry the `{{ .Tier }}` tag, so the transient `preferredModels` switch did not land (either the tag is not installed on any workspace profile, or the current model is unknown). Before doing any phase work, record the degradation on the bead so it is visible in the audit trail, then continue on best effort:

```bash
bd comment {{ .Target }} "⚠ tier-degraded [phase: {{ .Phase }}]: declared {{ .Tier }} but running on '{{ if .ModelName }}{{ .ModelName }}{{ else }}<unknown>{{ end }}' (tags: {{ if .ModelTags }}{{ range $i, $t := .ModelTags }}{{ if $i }}, {{ end }}{{ $t }}{{ end }}{{ else }}none{{ end }})."
```
{{- end }}
